  "tokenized_directions": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "{{ing_01|Milk-fed kid or lamb}} is carefully boned through the throat so as to create a paunch or bag."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "The intestines are preserved whole in a manner that one can blow or inflate them at the head in order to expel the excrements at the other end."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "The body is washed carefully and is filled with a liquid dressing."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "Thereupon tie it carefully at the shoulders, put it into the roasting pan, baste well."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "When done, boil the gravy with {{ing_03|milk}} and {{ing_02|pepper}}, previously crushed, and {{ing_04|broth}}, {{ing_05|reduced wine}}, {{ing_06|a little reduced must}} and also {{ing_07|oil}}."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "And to the boiling gravy add {{ing_08|roux}}."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "To play safe put the roast in a netting, bag or little basket and carefully tie together."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Add a little {{ing_09|salt}} to the boiling gravy."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "After this has boiled well three times, take the meat out, boil the {{ing_04|broth}} over again (to reduce it) incorporate with the above described liquor, adding the necessary seasoning."
    }
  ],
